{"type":"standard","title":"Lule language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Lule language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q12635889","titles":{"canonical":"Lule_language","normalized":"Lule language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Lule language</span></span>"},"pageid":3609047,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Lule_language_map.svg/330px-Lule_language_map.svg.png","width":330,"height":467},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Lule_language_map.svg/960px-Lule_language_map.svg.png","width":794,"height":1123},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1353984045","tid":"8324530d-4ee1-11f1-9139-12123567a4b2","timestamp":"2026-05-13T15:36:30Z","description":"Indigenous language of northern Argentina","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lule_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lule_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lule_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Lule_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lule_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Lule_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lule_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Lule_language"}},"extract":"Lule is an indigenous language of northern Argentina, which is now extinct. Campbell (1997) writes that in 1981 there was an unconfirmed report that Lule was still spoken by 5 families in Resistencia in east-central Chaco Province. It is unclear if it is the same language as Tonocoté.","extract_html":"<p><b>Lule</b> is an indigenous language of northern Argentina, which is now extinct. Campbell (1997) writes that in 1981 there was an unconfirmed report that Lule was still spoken by 5 families in Resistencia in east-central Chaco Province. It is unclear if it is the same language as <i>Tonocoté</i>.</p>"}